data: {"id":"chatcmpl-1793077409737","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1793077409,"model":"glm-5.3-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"id":"call4bbdbc03b9fa4b3089fb0e0c2a7a678e","type":"function","function":{"name":"write","arguments":"{\"content\":\"---\\nname: cv-jd-interview-screening\\ndescription: Match CV PDFs against a job description and produce a task-sized interview recommendation. Use when a user provides one or more resume PDFs plus job requirements and asks whether to recommend the candidate(s) for interview, or asks for evidence-anchored CV/JD matching.\\n---\\n\\n# CV × JD interview screening\\n\\nTurn one or more CV PDFs plus a job requirement into an interview recommendation (recommend / conditional / not-recommend) with page-anchored evidence. Produce a full evaluation report only when the user explicitly asks for one.\\n\\n## Step 1 — Extract CVs\\n\\nRun the extraction script on every PDF (batch is fine):\\n\\n```bash\\npython <skill_dir>/scripts/cv_extract.py cv1.pdf cv2.pdf --json extract_report.json\\n```\\n\\nEach result carries a content-hash `candidate_id` and per-page text, so renamed files and multi-PDF batches never mix candidates. Exit codes: 0 all extracted, 2 all failed, 3 partial.\\n\\n**Stop on explicit errors.** `file not found` / `empty file (0 bytes)` / `corrupt/unopenable PDF` / zero pages are reported as errors, never fabricated into an empty success. Tell the user which files failed and why; do not guess at their content. If a PDF has no extractable text layer (scanned image), say so and fall back to OCR/vision separately — do not silently return an empty page.\\n\\n## Step 2 — Semantic match (your judgment, not a script)\\n\\nCompare the CV evidence against each job requirement. This step is semantic and cannot be automated:\\n\\n- Quote the CV's own words for each requirement, with the page number (`P2`).\\n- Distinguish three levels: direct evidence / partial or adjacent evidence / no evidence in the CV. Absence of evidence is a gap to verify in interview, not automatic rejection or invention.\\n- Never use name, age, gender, ethnicity, or contact fields as fit criteria. Extract them for identity only.\\n- No keyword score or point total establishes hiring fit. School tier, exact tenure, industry equivalence, and contradictions need stated reasoning and appropriate hedging.\\n\\n## Step 3 — Validate literal quotes (when quoting matters)\\n\\nBefore delivering a recommendation that cites exact CV wording, verify each citation:\\n\\n```bash\\npython <skill_dir>/scripts/evidence_check.py claims.json\\n```\\n\\n`claims.json` is a JSON array: `[{\\\"file\\\": \\\"cv.pdf\\\", \\\"page\\\": 2, \\\"quote\\\": \\\"exact text from that CV\\\"}]`. Quotes are whitespace-normalized, so line breaks inside a PDF quote are fine. The checker fails (exit 2) on: quote absent, quote on a different page than claimed, out-of-range page, or any file-level extraction error — and reports the page(s) where the quote actually is. Fix the report before delivering.\\n\\n## Step 4 — Deliver task-sized output\\n\\n- Default deliverable: a short recommendation with per-requirement evidence (quote + page) and a clear verdict. Surface hard risks prominently (e.g. salary/location mismatch, missing mandatory evidence) as items to verify before or during interview.\\n- Full evaluation report only on request. No all-requirement ledger, no forced long format, no extra deliverables the user did not ask for.\\n- Match the user's language; keep their addressing preferences.\\n\\n## Boundaries\\n\\n- Explicit file errors are reported as failures, never laundered into success.\\n- Extraction/quote validation is mechanical; qualification interpretation stays semantic and human-reviewable.\\n- No protected-attribute-based filtering; no invented experience.\\n\",\"path\":\"/workspace/outputs/skill/SKILL.md\"}"}}]},"finish_reason":null}]}

